      "title": "Ukraine ‘offering Russia deal to halt attacks on civilian ships in Black Sea’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/13/ukraine-proposes-deal-with-russia-to-halt-attacks-on-civilian-ships-in-black-sea",
      "description": "<p>Kyiv reportedly suggested mutual agreement in attempt to reopen crucial grain corridor </p><p>Ukraine has proposed a deal with Russia for both sides to halt their attacks on civilian ships in the Black Sea in an apparent attempt to reopen a crucial grain corridor, Reuters reports.</p><p>Kyiv is said to have made the offer through a third party. Moscow has yet to respond, the news agency added. The busy waterway is a key export route for both Russia and Ukraine, used to transport grain and other vital foodstuffs worldwide.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/aug/13/ukraine-proposes-deal-with-russia-to-halt-attacks-on-civilian-ships-in-black-sea\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-13T17:13:33"
    },
    {
      "title": "World stares at food supply chaos as Russia attacks grain ships",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/world-stares-at-food-supply-chaos-as-russia-attacks-grain-ships-126081302109_1.html",
      "description": "Russian attacks on cargo vessels have sharply disrupted shipping from Odesa, threatening to trap millions of tonnes of grain during Ukraine's harvest season.",
